in this video i'll give you five of the  best ways to make money in animal  crossing without having to rely on  turnips so anytime you search online for  animal crossing money making tips  every list every video you find will  undoubtedly mention the stock market or  buying and selling turnips and it's true  buying and selling turnips is the most  efficient way to make large amounts of  money  fast in animal crossing but what about  those who maybe don't have time to check  prices multiple times every single day  or don't want to go through the hassle  of waiting in long lines to travel to  other islands or maybe you just forgot  to play on sunday which is the only day  to buy turnips  what are the other ways to make bells  today we're going to go over five of the  best ways to make bells fast and animal  crossing new horizons  people of the internet's retrorecon tour  here if this is your first time visiting  the channel we're all about helping you  connect and share stories with friends  and family through the power of video  games  and lately one of the best games to  connect and share with others has been  animal crossing new horizons now as i  mentioned in the opening today we're  focused on making money without turnips  now let's get started  number one selling fruit so one of the  best ways to start making money even  early on is to sell fruit now this is  going to start off very  simple but there's actually quite a bit  of depth to selling fruit that can net  you even more bells  to get started you simply shake trees  and sell the fruit now if you're new to  the game you may not know that each  island has its own  native fruit the fruit you have on your  island will sell for 100 bells each  at the time of this recording there are  currently six fruits in animal crossing  new horizons  apples cherries coconuts peaches  pears and oranges you can actually get  all fruits on your island by visiting  other islands now the reason you want  more than one fruit on your island is  because  non-native island fruits sell for 500  bells each  with the exception of coconuts which  sell for 250 bells each  still both are quite a big jump from the  100 bells you get with your native  fruits  now if you really want to maximize your  profits rather than immediately selling  any new fruits you obtain  you'll want to consider planting fruits  in the ground instead  after planting those fruits wait three  to four days and that  tree will bear fruit so the one fruit  you planted will end up being three  fruits in three to four days  then you can shake the tree which will  continue to bear fruit over and over  again  every few days it's definitely worth  your time to plant plenty of fruit trees  around your island  number two sell crafted items if you  start to find yourself with an over  abundance of materials such as rocks or  a certain kind of wood  consider crafting them into furniture  before selling  a lot of times players will simply sell  the extra materials but you'll get more  bang for your buck by using your diy  recipes to turn those spare materials  into furniture and don't forget to check  out the hot item of the day at nook's  cranny which  could end up being an item you can craft  which of course will  net you even more bells number three  catching bugs and fish okay look not  gonna lie to you guys this one is my  favorite way of making money in new  horizons for one catching bugs and fish  is just plain fun  i suggest using a guide or app so you  can target specific bugs and fish that  are worth the most  the acnh dot guide app is fantastic  there's also the animal crossing dot  fandom wiki  i've also created graphics that make it  easy to keep track of the new bugs and  fish  i'll include a link to all of these down  in the description below  now you may have the urge to sell your  bugs and fish right away at nook's  cranny but  unless you need the money fast you'll be  much better off by waiting for a visit  from flick or cj  they both pay 50 more than nook's cranny  so where nooks would buy a giant stack  for 10  000 bells flick will pay 15 000 bells  you can also use the nooks cranny  drop-off box overnight when your store  is closed however this is the worst of  the three methods as you'll only get 80  of the standard nooks cranny pricing of  course you can also sell the new sea  creatures which were added to the game  as part of the summer update  however there's no special vendor like  cj or flick to earn even more from your  efforts  and thanks to the recent changes in how  the game handles visitors to your island  you should never have to go too long  without having a visit from flick or cj  number four fossils fossils are a great  way to make money in new horizons and  require surprisingly little effort  the only challenge is to find where  they've spawned on your island  i've heard of as many as six spawning  per day but the most i've ever seen in a  day is  four usually i have at least three on my  island i do recommend you focus on  completing the museum before you start  selling fossils but of course that's  entirely up to you  the prices on fossils vary but it's  almost always worth your time  don't forget you'll always want to have  the fossils assessed first by blathers  at the museum before you take them to  nook's cranny my son actually tested out  a few weeks ago  you can sell the fossils by themselves  before they've been assessed but i think  it only net you something like 200 bells  it's very small  if you're getting value out of these  tips so far guys consider giving this  video a thumbs up  and if you'd like to see more animal  crossing tip videos on the channel hit  that subscribe button down below  and that's gonna take us right into  number five  nukazon this one is different from any  other on the list as you'll be partially  relying on the cooperation of another  human player you see nukazon is an  animal crossing marketplace managed  through discord  you can make lots of money doing tasks  that others may not have the time to do  themselves such as crafting fish bait or  maybe there's a particular furniture  item someone really wants to complete a  set and it just so happens you have the  item they need  there are many different ways to make  money here so if it sounds like  something you're interested in i'd  suggest checking out the link and  scrolling through some of the posts to  familiarize yourself with how things  work there now i have to stress with  this one you  are relying on another human player to  cooperate  and actually follow through giving you  the items or bells required as part of  your transaction  i've heard of some folks getting ripped  off but the vast vast majority of animal  crossing players i've met through my  stream discord reddit etc have all  been great to play and trade with i  should also stress we are not talking  about a real money exchange here we're  talking bells the in-game currency only  it's actually against nintendo's terms  of service to sell in-game goods for  real-world money now it also doesn't  have to be nukazon there are multiple  subreddits and discord groups out there  that do  very similar activities in fact if  you're looking to get started you're  more than welcome to join my discord as  well  i'll include links to all of these down  in the description below so this video  is all about making money without  turnips but now maybe you're curious as  to how turnips in the stock market  actually works in animal crossing  if you're thinking about giving it a try  check out the link on the top right side  of your page right now which is a link  to my full guide for how buying and  selling turnips works and new horizons  and if you're ready to start working  toward that five-star island score then  check out the link on the bottom right  side of your page  that's gonna be it for me today remember  we all have a story to tell  and your story matters thanks so much  for watching
 

